  2032	(A_Q)(X) as always).** Let X be a K+P position
  2033	with a king group Z satisfying (K1), (K2), the kings on {z, z′} and {w, w′}, and a context with D-model G (the pawn-only
  2034	game of Definition 1.5, with the e.p. flag as in the Remark). Let D = G ⊞ dud_D, with π sending a chess position to
  2035	(x, ω) and keeping the side to move. A *regular* position is one reachable from X by D-moves (matching context moves and
  2036	the two shuttles). Assume, at every regular position:
  2037	- **(V1a-ctx)** the legal context moves of the side to move are exactly G's options for that side, with the same
  2038	  resulting positions (e.p. through condition (E)); the shuttle is the pass;
  2039	- **(V2-ctx)** every decisive event of G leads to a P-win for its beneficiary (automatic for a pawn-only G scored by
  2040	  promotions);
  2041	and write **(Pun_s)** for: *every legal move of s that is neither a context move nor s's shuttle (a king move off the
  2042	shuttle, a Z-pawn move or capture) is decisively punished (Definition 2.5): the position after it is a P-win for s̄.*
  2043	- **(a) Win transfer.** Suppose r_D(x, ω, s) = W. Let Σ be a rank-lowering White strategy in D (by Lemma B it never
  2044	  passes) and N the set of chess positions arising when White plays Σ as chess moves and Black plays any legal D-move.
  2045	  If (Pun_Black) holds at the nodes of N with Black to move, then White wins X in P. White's king stays on its square, so
  2046	  only the two states (a, w), (a, w′) occur; White's shuttle and the square z′ are not used. The mirror statement for a
  2047	  Black win needs (Pun_White) at the nodes of N with White to move.
  2048	- **(b) Exactness.** If (Pun_White) and (Pun_Black) hold at all regular positions, the P-result of every regular
  2049	  position equals r_D(π(y)), draws included. In particular, if G has no decisive event, X is a draw in P.
